      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Labor's 2026 budget tax reforms trigger political firestorm over CGT, negative gearing and trusts",
      "summary": "The Albanese government's budget proposals to reduce the capital gains tax discount, limit negative gearing on existing properties, and tax discretionary trusts at a minimum 30% rate generated intense political controversy across the week. Albanese delivered an emotional defence of the changes at the Victorian Labor state conference on 23 May, framing them as 'pro-aspiration,' while facing a sustained backlash from small business groups, an AI meme campaign depicting him as a '47% silent partner,' criticism from NSW Premier Chris Minns, and polling showing Labor's primary vote under pressure. The government announced plans to legislate the CGT and negative gearing changes before the July winter break, while signalling openness to tweaks on trusts. The Greens signalled conditional support but demanded the grandfathering exemption be removed.",
