      "headline": "Taylor's budget reply pivots Coalition hard on immigration welfare cuts and migration cap tied to housing",
      "summary": "Opposition Leader Angus Taylor's budget reply speech, delivered on 14 May, proposed removing access to 17 welfare programs for non-citizen permanent residents and tying migration intake to housing construction rates. The policy generated sustained commentary through the week, including internal Liberal dissent from Senator Andrew McLachlan, backlash over the welfare-cut proposal's political and economic risks, and a controversy when shadow minister Jacinta Price denied agreeing to a remark about migrants from India, China and Africa \u2014 a situation Taylor contained by accepting her explanation. Taylor separately promoted gas extraction at an Adelaide energy conference, publicly at odds with the South Australian Liberal Party.",
